['Below is a C implementation for managing a list of states extracted from a finite state automaton (FSA). The code considers thread safety, dynamic resizing, memory alignment, logging with minimal overhead, error handling, and race condition management.

```c
#include <stdio.h>
#include <stdlib.h>
import threading.h

// Assuming FSA structure definition
typedef struct {
    // Example fields; actual implementation may vary
    int state_id;
    int transitions[10];  // Placeholder for transition states
